<title>USA: Typhoon moves from Marianas, ships still at risk.</title>
<headline>Typhoon moves from Marianas, ships still at risk.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>All typhoon warnings and watches for the northern Mariana islands, including Guam, have been dropped, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Typhoon Isa, with 120 mph winds, is tracking north-northwestward, away from the islands.</p>
<p>Further strengthening is expected as the system turns more northward, before beginning to weaken, WSC said. Shipping will be under extreme risk from this system.</p>
</text>
